{"id": 13, "ts": 1780600207.6642413, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I remain inclined to recommend Candidate\u202fC. Sarah highlighted C\u2019s flawless reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and the fact that he creates a positive crew atmosphere\u2014core safety criteria for long\u2011distance operations. While we know C has difficulty communicating ideas and an egocentric reputation, James just confirmed there are no concrete incidents showing this has harmed crew performance, and the positive atmosphere suggests any friction is being managed.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB, although very conscientious and strong under stress, has been reported to make nasty remarks toward colleagues and sometimes adopts the wrong tone. That directly undermines crew cooperation and professional communication, which are non\u2011negotiable for a cockpit environment. Even with his good stress resilience, the interpersonal issues pose a higher risk to safety than C\u2019s communication challenges.\nTherefore, given the current evidence, C still offers the strongest overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
