{"id": 28, "ts": 1780600320.5614698, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s thorough comparison and, after probing the gaps, I\u2019m still inclined to recommend Candidate\u202fC. While Sarah confirmed we have no concrete incident record to substantiate the \u201c100\u202f% reliability\u201d label, C\u2019s demonstrated ability to make correct decisions quickly, his excellent attention skills, and the fact that he consistently puts crew welfare above all suggest a high baseline of operational reliability. In contrast, the concerns about Candidate\u202fB\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks\u201d remain unsubstantiated\u2014James could not provide any specific incident or impact on safety\u2014so we cannot weigh that issue heavily against his strong stress\u2011resilience and conscientiousness. Candidate\u202fD\u2019s problem\u2011solving and responsibility are valuable, yet his moodiness and loner reputation raise unanswered questions about crew cooperation under long\u2011haul pressures. Candidate\u202fA\u2019s leadership and anticipatory skills are offset by unfriendly behavior and unhealthy habits that could affect reliability on extended flights. Given the totality of evidence, Candidate\u202fC still presents the most balanced fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role, provided we address his communication style during onboarding."}
